# SelfBubbles relay — example environment file.
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) next to relay.py and fill in. relay.py loads it only
# when python-dotenv is installed in the venv. Variables already set in the real
# environment (e.g. the LaunchAgent plist) always take precedence over this file.
# Never commit a real .env.
#
# Placeholders: a value that starts with change-me, changeme, replace-with or
# your- (in any capitalisation; the launchd example's CHANGE-ME is one) marks
# where a secret goes and is never used as one. The relay refuses to start
# while IMSG_TOKEN is a placeholder, and treats BB_PASSWORD, BEEPER_TOKEN,
# HA_TOKEN and MAPKIT_TOKEN as unset while they are; `relay.py --check` names
# each one. Do not choose a real secret that starts with one of those words.

# ---- relay core (relay.py) ----
# TCP port the FastAPI app listens on.
IMSG_PORT=8700
# Address to bind: 127.0.0.1 (loopback) when the HTTPS route (Tailscale Serve, a Cloudflare Tunnel) runs on this same Mac.
# Use 0.0.0.0 (the built-in default when this key is absent) only if the route reaches the relay over the LAN.
IMSG_BIND=127.0.0.1
# Comma-separated numbers that are *you* on other devices (excluded from chat matching).
IMSG_SELF=+15555550100,+15555550101
# Name of the phone macOS hands SMS/RCS sends to (e.g. OpenBubbles); shown in the chat header and composer warning.
TEXT_RELAY_LABEL="Pixel (…0100)"
# Path to the Messages database the relay polls.
IMSG_CHATDB=~/Library/Messages/chat.db
# Where the relay persists its cursor/state JSON (defaults to relay_state.json next to relay.py).
#IMSG_STATE=/absolute/path/to/relay_state.json
# Seconds between chat.db polls.
IMSG_POLL_SECONDS=2
# Shared secret required on every request (X-Imsg-Token header or ?token=).
# The value below is a placeholder and the relay will not start with it:
# replace it with a long random string (`openssl rand -hex 32` prints one).
IMSG_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Apple News link previews: the relay fetches apple.news links and the publisher
# page in the background to add an image/summary to the link card (cached in
# link_cache/). Set to 0 to disable all of that (no outbound fetches).
APPLE_NEWS_PREVIEWS=1

# ---- send engines (engines/) ----
# Outbound messages walk a chain of engines; the first that succeeds wins:
#   beeper       Google Messages chats (bp: guids) -- present when BEEPER_TOKEN is set
#   bluebubbles  iMessage via the BlueBubbles Private API -- present when BB_PASSWORD is set
#                (a placeholder does not count)
#   applescript  Messages.app scripting: text + files into existing chats only
#                (no tapbacks, no new chats) -- always present unless disabled below
#   imessage-cli edits a message you already sent, and does nothing else --
#                present when that tool is installed (IMESSAGE_CLI, further down)
# Without BB_PASSWORD the chain is just applescript: texts and files still go out.
# Override the order / membership of the engines that send with a comma-separated
# list of engine names. (The list cannot leave imessage-cli out: it sends nothing,
# and joins after the listed engines unless the list gives it a place. Its own
# switch is IMESSAGE_CLI=0.)
#SEND_ENGINES=bluebubbles,applescript
# Set to 0 to leave the AppleScript fallback out of the chain.
SEND_APPLESCRIPT_FALLBACK=1

# ---- edit and undo send (iMessage only, your own recent messages) ----
# Undo Send needs nothing here: it goes through BlueBubbles (BB_PASSWORD below,
# with the Private API). Editing does not work through BlueBubbles on macOS 27;
# the relay runs imessage-cli for it, Beeper's open-source command-line tool,
# which drives Messages.app through Accessibility. Optional:
#   brew install beeper/tap/imessage-cli
# The Python that runs the relay then needs Accessibility and Automation
# (System Settings > Privacy & Security). `imessage-cli authorize` shows the
# grants of the program that runs it, and asks for a missing one: from a
# terminal that is the terminal app, not the relay. The relay's own start-up
# table says "Accessibility NOT GRANTED" when its Python lacks that one, and
# /edit is then refused without starting the tool.
# The relay's use of the tool was checked with version 0.24.2; `brew pin
# imessage-cli` keeps `brew upgrade` from replacing it unseen.
# Unset, the relay looks for the tool in /opt/homebrew/bin, /usr/local/bin and
# on the PATH, and adds the engine when it is there. Set the path to name the
# binary yourself, or 0 to keep the engine off even where the tool is installed.
#IMESSAGE_CLI=/opt/homebrew/bin/imessage-cli

# ---- BlueBubbles (send engine + contacts + FaceTime) ----
# BlueBubbles server URL.
BB_URL=http://localhost:1234
# BlueBubbles server password (tapbacks, new chats, group icons, contact names
# and the FaceTime bridge need it; plain text and files go out through
# AppleScript without it). Commented out on purpose: copied as it is, this file
# gives the AppleScript-only chain. If you run BlueBubbles, uncomment the line
# and put the real password in place of the placeholder.
#BB_PASSWORD=your-bluebubbles-server-password

# ---- push notifications ----
# Path to a Firebase service-account JSON file; leave empty to disable FCM push.
FCM_CREDS=

# ---- Google Messages via Beeper Desktop (beeper.py) ----
# Beeper Desktop local API URL.
BEEPER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:23373
# Beeper Desktop local API token; leave empty to disable the Google Messages bridge.
BEEPER_TOKEN=
# Beeper account id prefix to surface (only this account is bridged).
BEEPER_GM_ACCOUNT=sh-gmessages
# mautrix-gmessages bridge DB, opened read-only to tell RCS from SMS.
BEEPER_BRIDGE_DB="~/Library/Application Support/bbctl/prod/sh-gmessages/mautrix-gmessages.db"
# Which phone each Google Messages account lives on, shown in the chat header; comma-separated "email=Label" pairs.
BEEPER_GM_ACCOUNT_LABELS="alice@example.com=Pixel (…0100),bob@example.com=Tablet (…0101)"

# ---- translation ----
# Always-resident MarianMT service for Latin-script -> English (unset = the
# relay's built-in default address; set it to advertise the translate feature
# to the app, so leave it commented out unless you run one).
#MARIAN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8701
# Ollama server used for non-Latin translation and as fallback.
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
# Ollama model name (unset = the relay's built-in default; set it to advertise
# the translate feature to the app).
#OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3:30b
# How long Ollama keeps the model in RAM after a request ("0" = unload now, "-1" = never).
OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE=5m

# ---- Home Assistant locations + map ----
# Home Assistant base URL.
HA_URL=http://homeassistant.local:8123
# Home Assistant long-lived access token; leave empty to disable locations.
HA_TOKEN=
# Comma-separated "Label=entity_id" pairs to show on the map.
HA_LOCATIONS=Alice=device_tracker.alice_phone,Bob=device_tracker.bob_car
# Apple MapKit JS token served to the app's /map page; leave empty to disable the map.
MAPKIT_TOKEN=

# ---- paths ----
# Where the FaceTime auto-admit rig writes its log (ft-auto.log), lock, trigger
# files and shots/. Defaults to the directory relay.py lives in. Caches
# (icons/, thumb_cache/, heic_cache/, audio_cache/, link_cache/) stay beside
# relay.py regardless.
#RELAY_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/data

# ---- FaceTime auto-admit (the author's rig; off by construction elsewhere) ----
# The Mac-side auto-admit helper (display-specific UI scripting; see docs) runs
# when a FaceTime link is minted ONLY if the Accessibility-granted loader app
# below exists. A fresh checkout has no such app, so the rig stays off and
# `relay.py --check` reports "off (helper app missing)". Set 0 to keep it off
# even with the app in place.
#FT_AUTOADMIT=0
# The loader app the rig runs in (reported by `relay.py --check`; never
# rebuilt). Defaults to FaceTimeAdmit.app beside relay.py.
#FT_ADMIT_APP=/absolute/path/to/FaceTimeAdmit.app

# ---- feature flags advertised to the app (GET /health "features") ----
# These set only what /health advertises. The app's own switches (Settings >
# Features) decide what it shows; only an app built with no FEATURES line and
# no baked-in relay URL takes its first values from here, once. The relay's
# routes stay mounted regardless. Unset = derived from the config above:
#   facetime  = BB_PASSWORD set          map   = MAPKIT_TOKEN and HA_TOKEN set
#   translate = OLLAMA_MODEL or MARIAN_URL set   voice = same as facetime
# 1/true/yes/on forces a feature on, anything else forces it off. Everything is
# off here so a fresh install starts with the plain inbox; delete a line to
# let the relay derive it.
FEATURE_FACETIME=0
FEATURE_MAP=0
FEATURE_TRANSLATE=0
FEATURE_VOICE=0
